A||||9||Homicidal||Rattling in the dashboard! GRR! Help!||||8||
Z||000000||Homicidal||11-26-2000||04:45 AM||||I have my sub in the front trunk, and I think over time it's loosened something or something came loose because now I get a rattling noise on the left speaker side everytime the bass hits (not fun when listening to rap/techno/r&b).  I notice if I apply pressure to the air vent grill or speaker cover, it stops, but the minute I take my hand away, it starts again.<P>I can't locate the rattle, it seems inside the dash.  So what is a quick remedy for this?<P>I plan to lay Dynomat on the front trunk, but that won't rid of the rattling from the dash.  <P>I was thinking of putting some form of putty or gummy substance in the hole where the speaker cover goes to hold it down (mock pressure if you will).  But this might prevent it from coming off later.....||||reg||8
Z||000001||overlord||11-26-2000||12:05 PM||||same exact problem here....||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-26-2000||01:06 PM||||inspect the grill itself. try it with the grill off. the thin areas of grill plastic is pretty brittle and cracks easily.||||reg||1
Z||000003||loafer87gt||11-26-2000||01:36 PM||||How do you get the stupid speaker grills off? I have a scratchy ticking sound coming from somewhere by my front speaker that drives me crazy. I have tried to take the speaker cover off before, but it doesn't want to come off, and I don't want to force it and break it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||11-26-2000||01:45 PM||||Far as I knoww, you just pry the speaker grilles up gently at the corners... they will pop out.  All of the front speaker grilles I've seen in Fieros have a plastic post in each corner, which plugs into a matching hole in the dash.<P>(All this from a guy that doesn't even knoww how to spell "knoww."  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">)<P> <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 11-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Smokey||11-26-2000||02:09 PM||||Are u sure you're left speaker ain't just blown?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000006||Homicidal||11-26-2000||02:12 PM||||I doubt it's the grill, the rattling just gets softer when I apply pressure to that general area.  <P>It totally stops when I hold the upper right corner of the speaker grill down.  I hear it when I take the grill off to, around the area.  When I hold the edge of the speaker down it also stops.  <P>What can I put in place of there to act as mock pressure? ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Homicidal||11-26-2000||02:40 PM||||I thought of that, but applying pressure to the area or to the edge of speaker wouldn't stop the rattling.  So it leads me to beleive something is just loose.||||reg||1
Z||000008||BAM-BAM||11-26-2000||03:14 PM||||    Pull up your speaker grill, while you are there check it out and see if it's cracked. To the windshield side of the speaker there is a 7MM bolt that holds the dash to the frame, check it. Also make sure that all your speaker anchors ar there, if one is missing or loose this could be your problem. Other than that, I would say you have a speaker problem. Just my 2<P> Peace, BAM OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> P.S. Be carefull popping the grills up, these dashes are old and they are brittle, especially the west coast cars. Pry gently or you could get into some trouble with a cracked dash. If that happens let me know, I can fix it for you.<P> Late!<p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 11-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||robertjay||11-26-2000||06:18 PM||||I just had the whole dash out on one of mine, and there really isn't much behind there.  Check to see if your speaker screws are still tight, possibly the white plastic "nuts" that they screw into could be broken.  I found some at the local auto parts store that fit great.  Possibly the grill for the defroster?  It is held on by 8 screws from the back.  Or you can check the outside vent grill, you have to remove the side pillar trim to get to it, but it is pretty easy.  Good luck.||||reg||1
